@startuml components
title M-UM1: component view within privileged process boundaries (unimplemented design)
left to right direction

actor "Configured caller\ninstaller / dispatcher / operator UID" as Caller
component "sudo\ntrusted root transition; exact path, no args" as Sudo
package "swarma-user-manager process\nroot; one helper-op/1 invocation (v0)" {
  component "Sudo entry validation\neffective UID + SUDO_UID + argv" as MEntry
  component "Closed helper decoder\n16 KiB / 5 s" as MDecode
  component "Caller policy\nrole / ownership / quota" as MPolicy
  component "Lock, journal and recovery\ncreate rollback / retire forward" as Recovery
  component "OS account backend\nmacOS dscl / Linux groupadd, useradd" as Accounts
  component "Descriptor-safe file operations\ntrusted directory descriptors; no-follow" as Files
  component "Retirement / archive / sweep\nquiescence; keys destroyed before walk\nmandatory secret exclusion; unknowns deleted" as Archive
  component "Egress adapter (v1)\npf / nftables; evidence matrix" as Firewall
  component "Authorised exec.stop\nreceipt + live identity; TERM / KILL\nproves process absence ONLY" as Stop
}
package "swarma-user-launcher process\nroot until privilege drop; one launch-op/1 invocation (v0)" {
  component "Sudo entry + closed decoder\n80 KiB / 5 s" as LEntry
  component "Launch validation\ncaller / generation / executor / home" as Launch
  component "Descriptor-safe executable / home opens\nno-follow; type / owner checks" as LFiles
  component "Receipt writer\natomic write before GID/UID drop" as Receipt
  component "Descriptor/environment reset\nFD3 plan; setsid; privilege drop; exec" as Exec
}
database "Root-owned configuration\nroles, ranges, archive policy, approved digests\nInstaller places it (§11)" as Config
database "Root-owned manager control state\nledger + allocation cursor; lock; journal; audit\nlauncher-written start receipts; v1 applied state" as State
database "OS directory service\naccount / primary-group records\nmanager-created; backend storage" as OS
folder "Account-owned homes\nroot-controlled home roots\nRoot quarantine + archives" as Homes
component "Kernel egress rules (v1)\nhelper-owned pf anchor / nftables table" as Kernel
component "curator-run -> harness\nagent account UID; immutable plan only" as Agent
component "swarma-credential-broker\nservice account; owns credentials / bindings / leases" as Broker
component "Profile proxy (v1)\ntrusted service account; verified listener" as Proxy

Caller --> Sudo : operation JSON on stdin
Sudo --> MEntry
Sudo --> LEntry
MEntry --> MDecode
MDecode --> MPolicy
MPolicy --> Config
MPolicy --> Recovery
Recovery --> State : one exclusive lock; journal before actions
Recovery --> Accounts
Recovery --> Archive
Recovery --> Firewall
Recovery --> Stop
Accounts --> OS
Accounts --> Files
Archive --> Files
Files --> Homes
Archive --> Broker : end generation binding
Firewall --> Kernel
Firewall --> Proxy : verify listener owner
Firewall --> State : publish applied state after successful apply
Stop --> State : matching root start receipt
Stop --> Agent : only verified process identity; success after absence
LEntry --> Launch
Launch --> Config
Launch --> State : same exclusive lock + recovery; active owned generation
Launch --> LFiles : no-follow executable / home
LFiles --> Homes : opened home as cwd
Launch --> Receipt
Receipt --> State
Receipt --> Exec
Exec --> Agent : verified exec; only standard FDs + FD3 plan
Agent --> Broker : fresh connection; lease
Broker --> State : reads ledger / v1 applied state; readability is not authority

note bottom of Recovery
  Refusal: invalid invocation/schema, role, ownership, quota, unmanaged objects,
  request_id conflict, unsafe path (§§2-6). Repeated same effect returns recorded
  result plus current state; next invocation recovers interrupted create/retire.
end note
note bottom of Launch
  Refusal: inactive/wrong-owner generation, unapproved executor, digest mismatch,
  existing execution receipt, failed privilege drop (§7).
  Post-receipt/pre-exec crash resolution and receipt retention: unspecified in spec §7.
  SH2+: dispatcher issues ticket; authenticated host presents it;
  this launcher redeems once under shared lock/journal, atomically with intent/receipt.
  Disabled until I4 publication; host role and ticket grammar unpublished (§§7, 14).
end note
note bottom of Stop
  No harness native-lock attestation (§4.7).
  Session-host recovery: fresh agent-UID runner checks native lock under closed fence;
  unknown result keeps parked (session-host §3.5).
end note
note bottom of Archive
  Configuration may add exclusions, never remove the mandatory secret class (§4.4.1).
  Destroy declared keys before any walk; failure/unknown prevents archive publication.
  Delete secret and unknown objects; required deletion failure keeps retiring.
  Archive only positively non-secret content/names/link metadata; root 0700, file 0600.
  Audit decisions/outcomes without secrets; unpublished formats in §14 question 6.
end note
note bottom of Firewall
  v1: refuse unsupported tuple; never report enforcement without whole-matrix evidence.
  Denial before first launch; retain until account/group removal (§8).
end note
note "Defining spec: [[../spec/helper.md#1-purpose §1 process split]], [[../spec/helper.md#2-invocation §§2-3 invocation/policy]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#46-lock-journal-and-idempotency §4.6 recovery]], [[../spec/helper.md#6-file-operations §6 paths]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 launcher]], [[../spec/helper.md#8-firewall-per-account-v1 §8 egress]].\nBoxes are conceptual responsibilities within binaries, not implemented classes or extra processes.\nCurrent: nothing implemented; v0 accounts/launcher, v1 egress, v2 grants (§13).\nv0/v1 refuse grants; v2 subject-bound chain checks target/time/revocation (§9); signature grammar open.\nSH1 internals: unspecified in spec §7; SH2+ launcher ticket gate closed until I4 publication (§§7, 14).\nDonor provisioning is a separate component; variant B disabled pending its spec (§1.1)." as Scope
Scope .. MEntry
@enduml
